#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:2
msgid "Watchdog timer"
msgstr "看门狗定时器"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:4
msgid ""
"A *watchdog timer* is a piece of hardware that resets the microcontroller if"
" the running script ever stops periodically poking it. The script \"feeds\" "
"the watchdog from somewhere it knows is running healthy code; if a bug, a "
"hang, or an unexpected exception ever keeps the camera from feeding the "
"watchdog within a configured timeout, the chip resets itself and the script "
"starts fresh."
msgstr ""
"*看门狗定时器*\\ 是一种硬件，如果正在运行的脚本停止定期触碰它，它就会复位微控制器。脚本从它确信正在运行健康代码的某处\"喂\"看门狗；如果某个 "
"bug、卡死或意外异常致使摄像头未能在配置的超时时间内喂狗，芯片就会自行复位，脚本随之重新开始。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:12
msgid ""
"On a deployed device with no human nearby to power-cycle it, this is the "
"difference between a transient bug that recovers in seconds and a brick that"
" needs a service call."
msgstr "在一台附近无人能够断电重启的已部署设备上，这就是一个能在数秒内自行恢复的瞬时 bug 与一台需要现场维修才能解决的变砖设备之间的区别。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:16
msgid ""
"A graph of a watchdog counter over time. The counter\n"
"starts at the timeout value, drops linearly toward\n"
"zero, and is reloaded to the timeout each time the\n"
"script calls feed(). After three successful feed()\n"
"calls, a fourth interval has no feed() and the counter\n"
"reaches zero, triggering an MCU reset."
msgstr ""
"一张随时间变化的看门狗计数器图。计数器\n"
"从超时值开始，线性下降趋向\n"
"零，并在脚本每次调用 feed() 时重新装填为超时值。在三次成功的 feed()\n"
"调用之后，第四个间隔没有 feed()，计数器\n"
"到达零，触发 MCU 复位。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:16
msgid ".. image:: ../figures/watchdog-countdown.svg"
msgstr ".. image:: ../figures/watchdog-countdown.svg"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:24
msgid ""
"The watchdog counter ticks down from its timeout. Each ``feed()`` reloads "
"it; if it reaches zero, the chip resets."
msgstr "看门狗计数器从其超时值开始递减。每次 ``feed()`` 都会重新装填它；如果它到达零，芯片就会复位。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:28
msgid "The machine.WDT class"
msgstr "machine.WDT 类"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:30
msgid ""
":class:`machine.WDT` enables the watchdog and exposes a single method, "
":meth:`~machine.WDT.feed`. Once started, the watchdog cannot be stopped -- "
"the only ways out are feeding it on schedule or letting it reset the chip:"
msgstr ""
":class:`machine.WDT` 启用看门狗并提供唯一一个方法 :meth:`~machine.WDT.feed`\\ "
"。一旦启动，看门狗就无法停止——唯一的出路是按时喂它或让它复位芯片："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:45
msgid ""
"The ``timeout`` is in milliseconds. The right value depends on how long the "
"longest legitimate iteration of the main loop takes, with comfortable "
"headroom -- a 100-ms loop with a 2-s timeout has plenty of margin for a slow"
" iteration without nuisance resets."
msgstr ""
"``timeout`` 以毫秒为单位。正确的值取决于主循环最长的合理迭代需要多久，并留出充裕的余量——一个 100 毫秒的循环配 2 "
"秒的超时，对于一次较慢的迭代有充足的余量，又不会产生误复位。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:52
msgid "Where to call feed()"
msgstr "在哪里调用 feed()"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:54
msgid ""
"Where ``feed()`` lives is the critical design decision; the watchdog only "
"catches bugs in the parts of the code that do *not* run between feeds."
msgstr "``feed()`` 放在何处是关键的设计决策；看门狗只能捕获那些在两次喂狗之间\\ *不*\\ 运行的代码部分中的 bug。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:58
msgid ""
"**Call from the main loop, at the top or bottom.** The most common pattern. "
"The watchdog catches anything that hangs the main loop -- a deadlock, an "
"infinite ``while``, a peripheral that never returns -- and resets the chip "
"back into the loop."
msgstr ""
"**从主循环调用，放在顶部或底部。** 最常见的模式。看门狗会捕获任何使主循环卡死的情况——死锁、无限 ``while``\\ "
"、永不返回的外设——并将芯片复位回循环中。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:62
msgid ""
"**Do not call from an interrupt handler.** The point of the watchdog is to "
"catch hangs in the *normal* code path. An ISR that fires regardless of "
"whether the main loop is stuck would keep feeding a watchdog that *should* "
"be triggering."
msgstr ""
"**不要从中断处理程序中调用。** 看门狗的意义在于捕获\\ *正常*\\ 代码路径中的卡死。无论主循环是否卡住都会触发的 ISR，会持续喂一个\\ "
"*本该*\\ 触发的看门狗。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:66
msgid ""
"**Do not call from inside a long blocking operation.** A network request or "
"sensor read that takes ten seconds is exactly the kind of hang the watchdog "
"should catch. Putting ``feed()`` inside it defeats the protection."
msgstr ""
"**不要在长时间阻塞操作内部调用。** 一个耗时十秒的网络请求或传感器读取，正是看门狗应当捕获的那种卡死。把 ``feed()`` "
"放在其中会使这种保护失效。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:71
msgid ""
"A guideline that works for most programs: feed once per main loop iteration,"
" with the timeout set to several times the expected loop duration. If a "
"single iteration legitimately needs longer than the timeout -- a deliberate "
"calibration phase, say -- structure that phase as a series of smaller chunks"
" with ``feed()`` between them, or change the timeout with "
":meth:`~machine.WDT.timeout_ms` (where supported) before entering it."
msgstr ""
"对大多数程序适用的一条准则：每次主循环迭代喂一次，并将超时设置为预期循环时长的数倍。如果单次迭代确实需要超过超时的时间——比如一个有意的校准阶段——则将该阶段拆分为一系列较小的块，块与块之间穿插"
" ``feed()``\\ ，或在进入该阶段之前用 :meth:`~machine.WDT.timeout_ms`\\ （在受支持的情况下）更改超时。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:81
msgid "Availability"
msgstr "可用性"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:83
msgid ""
"The watchdog is exposed on most OpenMV cams but not all -- the hardware is "
"present on every part, but the Python API is not yet wired up everywhere. "
"Check the :doc:`/openmvcam/quickref` or attempt to construct a "
":class:`~machine.WDT` and catch the ``AttributeError`` if it is not "
"supported."
msgstr ""
"看门狗在大多数 OpenMV 摄像头上都有提供，但并非全部——硬件在每个部件上都存在，但 Python API 尚未在所有地方接通。请查看 "
":doc:`/openmvcam/quickref`\\ ，或尝试构造一个 :class:`~machine.WDT` 并在不受支持时捕获 "
"``AttributeError``\\ 。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/watchdog.rst:89
msgid ""
"Even on cams where :class:`~machine.WDT` is not exposed, a field-deployed "
"device can use a soft equivalent -- a separate task or main-loop step that "
"monitors progress and triggers :func:`machine.reset` if anything looks "
"wedged. It is less robust than a hardware watchdog (a wedged interrupt "
"handler can take down the soft monitor too) but it covers the same cases at "
"the application level."
msgstr ""
"即使在未提供 :class:`~machine.WDT` "
"的摄像头上，现场部署的设备也可以使用软件等效方案——一个独立的任务或主循环步骤，用于监控进度并在出现异常卡滞时触发 "
":func:`machine.reset`\\ 。它不如硬件看门狗稳健（一个卡住的中断处理程序也可能拖垮软件监控器），但它在应用层面覆盖了相同的情况。"
